hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1171","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala al-Sadfi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, H. Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb, Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, and Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah told him, that Abd Al-Rahman bin Abdul-Qari said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sleeps on the side of his party or on the Some of it, which he recited between the dawn prayer and the noon prayer, was written down for him as if he had recited it at night.” Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz Al-Ayli told us, Salama told me, on the authority of Aqeel, Ibn Shihab said: Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid and Ubayd Allah told me Bin Abdullah, that Abdul Rahman bin Abdul, said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God Almighty be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: the same"
